# Feature documentation (Documentations MD)

For **every new feature** or **meaningful change** to existing behavior, maintain documentation in `Documentations MD/`.

## Required workflow

1. **Find or create** a feature doc in `Documentations MD/` (kebab-case, e.g. `expense-batch-review.md`).
2. **Update that file** with what changed, why, key files, migrations, and test steps.
3. **Update `Documentations MD/index.md`** — table row + revision log entry (date, author/agent, summary).
4. Use `Documentations MD/_DOC_TEMPLATE.md` when creating a new doc.

Do **not** skip docs because the change feels small. If it affects users, reviewers, or deploy steps, it gets a doc update.

## Doc content (minimum)

- **Purpose** — what the feature/fix does
- **Status** — draft | in progress | deployed | superseded
- **Last updated** — ISO date at top of file
- **Revision log** — dated entries at bottom of each feature file
- **Key files** — paths touched
- **Database** — migrations to run (reference filename only; user runs SQL manually)
- **Test plan** — how to verify

## Index maintenance

`Documentations MD/index.md` is the single catalog. Always update when adding or materially editing a doc:

| Column | Content |
|--------|---------|
| ID | Short slug (e.g. `DOC-014`) |
| Title | Human-readable name |
| File | Path under repo root |
| Last updated | From file header or git |
| Status | Same as doc status |
| Summary | One line |

Add a **Revision log** block in `index.md` for each index change.

## Legacy `docs/` folder

Older files may still live in `docs/`. When touching those features, **copy or consolidate** into `Documentations MD/` and note the move in both the index and the legacy file header (`> Superseded by: Documentations MD/...`).

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD — ship custom form field fix, no doc
(only code changes)

✅ GOOD — after implementing review dialog fix
- Update Documentations MD/custom-form-fields-review-display.md (Pass 9 section)
- Add index row + revision log in Documentations MD/index.md
```

```text
❌ BAD — new Reports export feature, doc only in PR description

✅ GOOD
- Create Documentations MD/reports-csv-export.md from _DOC_TEMPLATE.md
- Register in index.md as DOC-0xx
```
